# Ford Zodiac Mk III four-door saloon, 1962-1966.
#
# The Mk III Zodiac: the Zephyr shell with four headlamps in a horizontal-bar
# grille, the Zodiac script and the higher trim. The front photograph in the
# pack is a different, blue car; the side and rear govern.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Zodiac
#
# Dimensions 4.642 x 1.753 x 1.441 m, wheelbase 2.718 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation; the front and rear
# three-quarters show the four-lamp grille and the tail.
#
# Colours: grade (d) for a full list, grade (c) for Ambassador Blue. The
# range otherwise used the Ford corporate palette; Ambassador Blue, Ermine
# White, Monaco Red and Lombard Grey are used. Weights 9, 8, 7, 6, total 30,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 155 km/h. Comfort 65/428, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 65. Classes 1,2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1962 intro, retires staggered 1982-1985.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-zodiac-mk3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/ford-zodiac-mk3.dae. References:
# citycars/references/ford-zodiac-mk3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear door and C-pillar changes are understated, and
# the rear finisher is too flat. At 128 px the four-lamp horizontal-bar grille,
# Zodiac script and finned tail read as a Zodiac Mk III.


obj=citycar
name=FordZodiacMk3(AmbassadorBlue)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=9
intro_year=1962
intro_month=4
retire_year=1985
retire_month=6
speed=155
length=3
class=1,2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=65
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=428

